+## Follow-up extraction candidate (pending complete release acceptance)
+
+The HTML entry remains `index.html`; browser composition remains `src/main.js`. Build-time page rendering starts in `tools/page-templates.mjs`, using the same page/component owners that guarded React mounts enhance later. Native first-entry adapters remain intentional under ADR001; there is no eager second application root.
+
+- Shared UI: `GunContext`, `PreferenceToggle`, `DrillSetupField`, `DrillSetupDelayMode` and `DrillSetupDelayRange` join the existing page heading/run/review owners. Settings-only rows/sections stay inside its feature.
+- Live Listen: `LiveModePanel`, `LiveCapturePanel` and `LiveResultPanel` compose its page; the parent owns state/actions. Existing History list/evaluation/progress components remain its owners.
+- Preferences: `src/preferenceCoordinator.js` holds the single preference record and injected actions. Gun workflows/cache/epoch live in `src/gunLibraryCoordinator.js`; optional library presentation loads from `src/gunLibraryView.js` only on library navigation.
+- Persistence: `src/storage.js` preserves the public API. `src/storage/library.js` implements runtime operations, `database.js` owns schema/migrations/transactions, and pure validation modules have no platform dependencies. Explicit backup import loads `restoreBackup.js`; validation still finishes synchronously before the atomic replacement transaction. Formats1–4 and schema4 are unchanged. Original logical-owner coverage floors retain the entire extracted denominator.
+- Release assets: `tools/build-identity.mjs` fingerprints source/public inputs; `workers/sw.js` verifies a complete release before marking its cache usable. Public tabs are never automatically reloaded; normal waiting-worker activation preserves current sessions. No IndexedDB cache purge occurs.
+
+Each visual component retains its own source, CSS, test and public entry. Source-only moves preserve the reviewed screenshots/GIFs; complete pinned browser and original performance acceptance still gate publication. The machine-readable [component map](component-map.json) and [application sitemap](application-sitemap.md) remain the maintained ownership/route indexes.
